<title>USA: U.S. Robotics technology used by Web America.</title>
<headline>U.S. Robotics technology used by Web America.</headline>
<dateline>SKOKIE, Ill. 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Robotics Corp said Wednesday that Web America Networks of Dallas will provide Internet access service across the country using U.S. Robotics Total Control remote access services and its new x2 technology.</p>
<p>Last month, U.S. Robotics said it began shipping its x2 modem technology, which allows Internet connections at 56 kilobits per second, or roughly twice as fast over telephone lines as current modems.</p>
<p>((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
